 "name": "Tempester n°38: the machine reports Level, Pan, Delay Send, Delay Time, Delay Repeats, tempo, Swing, Volume, Distort and Compress (NRPN 230-239 on Remote Pad OUT)",
 "image": "Main 1.5.0.2",
 "input_sha256": "86aaf7ca41be60140f11dd4fed84bffed2590746dcb267d4e9947128974336be",
 "explanation": "Dependency: requires n°9b (patch/nrpn_emission.json) for its SENDCC routine at 0x9d07a504. Bug: the remote panel (n°23) moves Level, Pan, Delay Send, Delay Time, BPM... on the machine, but turning those knobs on the machine moved nothing in the app: they are neither sound parameters (n°9b) nor beat-wide positions (n°29), and the stock OS sends no CC. Values, where [routine]'s knob handlers store them (read only): 0 Level, 1 Pan, 2 Delay Send of the selected pad = mixer bytes +1, +2, +3 of [address] + beat * 0x180 + pad * 4 (beat = UI object +0x13C [address], pad = +0x52 [address]); 3 Delay Time, 4 Delay Repeats = beat bytes +0x32, +0x33 of [address] + beat * 0x294 (Shift + encoder 9, Shift + absolute control 6 Pan); 5 tempo x 10 rounded (float [address]), 6 Swing, 7 Volume, 8 Distort ([address], as given to [routine]), 9 Compress ([address], as given to [routine]). Fix: (1) POLL (0x9d079648), in place of the main loop's call of [routine] at [address] (every pass of both branches; made first): reads the 10 values, compares them with the last values sent ([address], 10 u16) and sends at most 4 changed items per pass as NRPN 230 + item (CC 99 = 1, CC 98 = 0x66 + item, CC 6 = value >> 7, CC 38 = value & 0x7f, through SENDCC: DIN B0|ch then USB) on Remote Pad OUT, only when it is not Off and the DIN send ring holds at most 16 bytes; coalesced (latest value), Off keeps the differences; the first pass after boot takes the state as sent; while following MIDI clock ([address] = 2 or 3) the tempo is not reported unless requested. (2) No echo: the CC jump table entries of CC 12 and CC 13 ([address], [address]) go to CC12 / CC13, which make the stock call ([routine] / [routine] of the value) and record the result as sent, then return through the default case [address]. The remote panel (n°21, n°23) is reported, as by n°9b and n°29. (3) REQ, at [address] in [routine] (replaced store redone, then back to [address]): CC 107 on Remote Pad IN (n°22's full-state request) marks the 10 items ([address] forced bits, [address] request flag). The machine accepts no NRPN 230-239 (n°9a refuses numbers >= 200, n°23 takes 200-213 and 220-229): a report sent back changes nothing. RAM [address]-[address] in the .bss hole [address]-[address], reached by no code in 1.6.3.0 (tools/gp_map.py), main loop only. Code at 0x9d079648-0x9d079993 (free flash, all 0xFF in 1.5.0.2 and 1.6.3.0).",
